# .vexpignore — paths excluded from vexp's code index/ranking (gitignore syntax).
# These files STAY in git; they're just kept out of run_pipeline's ranked context so
# source code isn't crowded out by process/release prose.
# Standard: vexp-context-engine @ v1.0.0 (crzynet/homelab-configs).
#
# vexp's built-in excludes already cover: node_modules, .git, dist, .next, target,
# __pycache__, .vexp. The SecurityFilter already drops .env / credentials. Only add
# things that ARE committed source-tree files but make poor ranked context.

# Release-note prose — large, churny, never useful as live code context.
CHANGELOG.md
docs/CHANGELOG-*.x.md

# Archived (squashed) migrations — reference only, not part of the active chain.
backend/migrations/archive/

# Other common candidates (uncomment if spec docs start crowding out code):
# docs/**/*.md
# (this project does not use the handoff-prompt workflow, so no prompts/done/)
